   468	## Appetite and non-goals
   469	
   470	One Build. Not in this Intent:
   471	
   472	- concurrent Builds, per-Build locks, two logins at once (order 8);
   473	- pinned engine generations (order 6);
   474	- process-group custody (order 7);
   475	- continuing or adopting a stopped Candidate;
   476	- rebase or re-verify on a moved `main`;
   477	- warm seeding;
   478	- a publish-later command, prune and orphan cleanup;
   479	- pruning per-path harness state.
   480	
   481	The write boundary (outcome 13) confines **writes** of Build role process trees.
   482	The following are outside it:
   483	- Shaping sessions. Their containment is BLD-12's Shaping half, in the
   484	  `headless-shaping-and-question-inbox` row.
   485	- Reads and network, which stay open.
   486	- The controller and its verification children (`make check` and targets). The
   487	  controller has to write, and fixture Builds inside them must apply their own
   488	  profile.
   489	- Kernel protection of the Build's own Approved copy inside the Candidate. It
   490	  stays protected by today's approved-mutation stop (detect and stop), because
   491	  the Shaper's rule names the worktree as the boundary.
   492	- A Linux mechanism (DST-03).
   493	
   494	Also out: changes to hooks, Claude settings, prompts, `Makefile`, the catalog or
   495	`.kogen/config.yaml`; Jev, Review independence, retry allowances; any new paid
   496	target (the existing `live-reviewer-rework` is selected, see Evidence ownership).
