   618	
   619	- `check` owns everything deterministic: topology, harness-home and credential
   620	  wiring, routing sentinels, controller verification in the Candidate,
   621	  same-Candidate rework in the fake lifecycle, Shaping during a Build,
   622	  publication and refusal, retention, records and the commands, plus the write
   623	  boundary's profile, every refusal and allowed write (real `sandbox-exec`, fake
   624	  roles), the Codex scope denials and every fail-closed and inherited case.
   625	- `live-shape-to-build` owns the Claude Code provider-only observables:
   626	  - a real Claude Code Developer logs in through the scope reference from a
   627	    per-Build config dir;
   628	  - its session resumes there in the Candidate cwd after a controller-failed
   629	    verification;
   630	  - the real Reviewer on the default route's Reviewer harness (Claude Code
   631	    while `default_route` stays `claude`; the paid fixture copies the
   632	    repository's `.kogen/config.yaml`) runs in the same Candidate. The Codex
   633	    Reviewer's Candidate cwd and per-Build operation root are proved offline
   634	    only;
   635	  - the fixture's `main` is fast-forwarded and the Candidate is removed;
   636	  - the real interactive Shape session before it still uses the scope's own
   637	    config dir with the same login;
   638	  - the real Claude Code Developer (fresh and resumed) and Reviewer run to
   639	    acceptance inside the write boundary, and a write from their process trees
   640	    into the fixture's control checkout and its Git refs is refused (scenario
   641	    `role-write-boundary`).
   642	- `live-reviewer-rework` owns the one Codex provider-only observable. Its nested
   643	  Build already runs the hybrid route every batch Build uses, and its real Codex
   644	  Reviewer returns both verdicts inside the boundary, with rollouts, login refresh
   645	  and bookkeeping in the granted Codex scope (scenario `codex-roles-inside-boundary`).
   646	  It is not a new target. Its support, `test/support/root_profile_audit.ex` and
   647	  `test/support/live_reviewer_rework_fixture.ex`, is edited here, and no other target
   648	  runs a real Codex role through a Kogen Build. DIRECTION D8 allows a second paid
