     5	- id: self-hosting-running-controller
     6	  scenario_ids: [controller-judges-candidate, same-candidate-rework]
     7	  description: >-
     8	    The installing Build runs under the then-main controller in the one checkout. That
     9	    controller reads `.codex/hooks.json` (byte-compared PreToolUse command,
    10	    lib/kogen/verification_policy.ex:14,59-85 at 363c20af), `priv/kogen/claude_code/settings.json` (passed by
    11	    path, lib/kogen/harness/claude.ex:26,164-165 at 363c20af), the role prompts, the Makefile, the catalog and
    12	    `.kogen/config.yaml` from disk while it runs. Build cFnHwg7P2oNe1wMMnK7jxeMH passed both paid
    13	    targets and then died at the rework launch because its Candidate rewrote the hook commands.
    14	    Mitigation: none of those paths is in may_change_guarded_paths, and controller-judges-candidate
    15	    asserts they stay byte-identical. The controller may also lazily load modules from `_build/dev`
    16	    that a Developer `mix compile` in dev rewrote (evidence/engine-stability-probe-2026-09-23.md);
    17	    the Developer compiles only in the test environment or in fixture build paths, and pinned
    18	    generations (ROADMAP order 6) remove the hazard. Nobody may write in the checkout while this
    19	    Build runs.
    20	
    21	- id: undocumented-secure-storage-variable
    22	  scenario_ids: [per-build-harness-home]
    23	  description: >-
    24	    The per-Build Claude Code home depends on `CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR`, an undocumented
    25	    variable read in the managed 2.1.281 binary
    26	    (evidence/harness-home-credential-probe-2026-09-25.md). A later runtime could rename or drop
    27	    it. Failure is closed and loses nothing: Build readiness runs `claude auth status` with the
    28	    Build's own environment and stops with "not logged in" before any model launch, and no Keychain
    29	    item or scope file is touched. The Claude Code runtime-upgrade workflow gains the re-probe of
    30	    cases A, D2 and F. Fallback if it disappears: CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR stays the scope and only Codex
    31	    keeps a per-Build operation root, a documented regression of this outcome.
    32	
    33	- id: shared-login-refresh
    34	  scenario_ids: [per-build-harness-home, shaping-during-build]
    35	  description: >-
    36	    A Shaping session (scope as its config dir) and a Build (per-Build config dir) use one OAuth
    37	    login at the same time. Claude Code serializes refreshes with `.oauth_refresh.lock` in the
    38	    secure-storage dir, which is the scope for both, and re-reads the Keychain item (30 s cache);
    39	    this is the same mechanism several concurrent sessions of one scope already use. A copied
    40	    credential would fork the refresh token and can log the other session out, which is why
    41	    nothing is copied. Codex refreshes `auth.json` in its scope exactly as today.
    42	
    43	- id: candidate-worktree-lifecycle
    44	  scenario_ids: [candidate-creation, publication-unmoved-main, publication-refused, failure-retention, candidate-commands]
    45	  description: >-
    46	    Kogen creates worktrees and harness homes for many projects under one Kogen directory,
    47	    registered in each project's Git metadata. Unclear ownership could delete another project's
    48	    work or a foreign worktree, keep stale Candidates forever, or reuse one by accident.
    49	  ownership:
    50	    - paths: "<workspaces-root>/<project-id>/<slug>-<build-id>/ and its registration under the control repository's .git/worktrees/"
    51	      when_exists: "Admission refuses a pre-existing path, registered worktree or branch with that name and never reuses it."
    52	      owner_after_creation: "The Build controller that created it, bound by its owner record (build id, control root, branch, base commit A)."
    53	      owner_during_operation: "The controller owns topology; the Developer may edit Candidate files; verification, Jev and Review read them."
    54	      permitted_mutation: "Developer edits inside the Candidate; the controller writes the Approved copy, Complete package and commit. Automatic removal only after successful publication (git worktree remove without --force). Otherwise only mix kogen.candidates.remove on the Shaper's request."
    55	      validation: "Every removal checks the path is under <workspaces-root>/<project-id>/, matches its owner record and is registered in this control repository. Running Candidates, and accepted-unpublished ones without --discard-accepted, are refused."
    56	      git_state: "Outside the control tree; listed by the control repository's git worktree list until removed; control status unaffected."
    57	      upgrade_behavior: "Worktrees without a Kogen owner record, including .kogen/runtime/build-worktrees/** from earlier experiments, are foreign and never touched; no migration."
    58	    - paths: "refs/heads/kogen/<slug>/<build-id>"
    59	      when_exists: "Admission refuses an existing branch with that name."
    60	      owner_after_creation: "The Build controller, then the Shaper through the Candidate commands."
    61	      owner_during_operation: "The controller makes the one publication commit; the Developer commits nothing."
    62	      permitted_mutation: "git branch -d after successful publication; git branch -D only through remove under the guards above."
    63	      validation: "An accepted commit not reachable from the admitted branch is deleted only with --discard-accepted."
    64	      git_state: "Local branch; never pushed."
    65	      upgrade_behavior: "Branches from earlier experiments (kogen/build/<intent-id>/<id>) are foreign and untouched."
    66	    - paths: "<workspaces-root>/<project-id>/candidates/<build-id>.json"
    67	      when_exists: "An existing owner record for the new build id refuses admission; a record naming a different control root under this project id stops admission."
    68	      owner_after_creation: "The Build controller writes it and updates the status at every exit; the Candidate commands read and delete it."
    69	      owner_during_operation: "Outside the Candidate; roles have no reason to touch it; not hostile containment."
    70	      permitted_mutation: "Status transitions running -> stopped/accepted-unpublished, or deletion on publication or removal. A running status counts only while the project's build lock is held by a live process."
    71	      validation: "Malformed or mismatched records are reported and skipped, never used to delete a path."
    72	      git_state: "Not in any repository."
    73	      upgrade_behavior: "Versioned schema field; no earlier records exist."
    74	    - paths: "<workspaces-root>/<project-id>/harness/<build-id>/ (claude/ as the Build's CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, codex/ as its Codex operation root)"
    75	      when_exists: "Admission refuses a pre-existing harness home for the new build id."
    76	      owner_after_creation: "The Build controller; Claude Code and Codex write their own session state inside it."
    77	      owner_during_operation: "Every role launch of this Build and nothing else; it never holds a credential."
    78	      permitted_mutation: "Harness-native writes during the Build. Kept after publication as session evidence; removed only with a retained Candidate by mix kogen.candidates.remove."
    79	      validation: "Removal uses the same owner-record and path checks as the worktree; a home without an owner record is never deleted by Kogen."
    80	      git_state: "Not in any repository."
    81	      upgrade_behavior: "No earlier homes exist; accumulation after publication is parked with Candidate prune (SHAPE_CANDIDATE_PRUNE.md)."
    82	    - paths: "Kogen login scopes: ~/Library/Application Support/Kogen/claude/accounts/** and ~/Library/Application Support/Kogen/codex/accounts/**"
    83	      when_exists: "Referenced by path only: CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR for Claude Code, CODEX_HOME for Codex."
    84	      owner_after_creation: "The Shaper through mix kogen.{claude,codex}.login; the harness runtimes own their contents."
    85	      owner_during_operation: "Build roles reach them only through the runtime's own credential lookup and refresh lock; the write boundary lets a role write only the Claude refresh lock and the Codex scope minus its refused and Kogen-owned entries (role-write-boundary, codex-roles-inside-boundary)."
    86	      permitted_mutation: "Kogen never creates, copies, links, moves or renames anything in a scope for this Intent; harness-native writes (token refresh, Codex rollouts) continue as today."
    87	      validation: "per-build-harness-home snapshots the scope's file list before and after a fake Build and asserts no Kogen-made change."
    88	      git_state: "Not in any repository."
    89	      upgrade_behavior: "Existing logins keep working unchanged; no migration."
    90	
    91	- id: approved-copy-in-candidate
    92	  scenario_ids: [candidate-creation, publication-unmoved-main, publication-refused, shaping-during-build]
    93	  description: >-
    94	    Roles read the Approved package in their cwd, but it is ignored and not in the worktree
    95	    checkout. A missing copy breaks roles, and an editable copy used as authority would let a
    96	    Developer rewrite the contract.
    97	  ownership:
    98	    - paths: "<Candidate>/.kogen/intents/approved/<slug>/"
    99	      when_exists: "Written at admission from the controller's frozen in-memory Approved bytes; a pre-existing path means the Candidate is not fresh and admission refuses."
   100	      owner_after_creation: "The controller."
   101	      owner_during_operation: "Read-only for roles; the frozen bytes remain authority, and publication packages from them."
   102	      permitted_mutation: "None by roles. The controller removes it with the Candidate."
   103	      validation: "The existing approved-mutation check applies to this copy; a mismatch is an integrity failure."
   104	      git_state: "Ignored in the Candidate; control's own Approved copy is unchanged until successful publication removes it."
   105	      upgrade_behavior: "None."
   106	
   107	- id: shared-cwd-assumptions
   108	  scenario_ids: [candidate-routing, publication-unmoved-main]
   109	  description: >-
   110	    About fifteen offline test files run Build.run inside File.cd!(repo) and assert on repo's
   111	    HEAD. They keep passing if Build silently works in the invoking checkout, so they must also
   112	    assert that a Candidate existed and was the role cwd. Their test-reliability source_sha256
   113	    bindings must be refreshed with scripts/check/refresh_test_reliability_sources.py.
   114	
   115	- id: boundary-breaks-existing-fixtures
   116	  scenario_ids: [role-write-boundary, write-boundary-fails-closed, shaping-during-build]
   117	  description: >-
   118	    Every fake-harness Build in check now runs its fake roles inside a real Seatbelt profile. Any
   119	    existing fixture whose fake role, fake hook or helper script writes outside the Candidate, the
   120	    harness home or the Build temp dir gets EPERM (known at 363c20af: the midbuild-config-mutation.sh
   121	    hook of two_outer_resumptions_test.exs and the control-side writes of shaping-during-build). In
   122	    the 2026-09-19 containment attempt, 47 tests failed when fixture Builds ran inside an outer
   123	    profile. Mitigation: the controller's make check is unconfined, so fixture Builds apply their own
   124	    profile; moved writes go to the trusted test process; no grant is widened and no fake executable
   125	    is special-cased; the INTENT Developer notes list the rule. Inside the Developer's own shell,
   126	    fixture Builds run inherited, and probe 9 showed today's whole suite gives the same result inside
   127	    the profile.
   128	
   129	- id: seatbelt-interface-deprecated
   130	  scenario_ids: [role-write-boundary, write-boundary-fails-closed]
   131	  description: >-
   132	    `sandbox-exec` and SBPL are undocumented and marked deprecated, although Apple still ships them
   133	    and uses the same kernel profiles. A macOS release could remove or change them. Failure is
   134	    closed: a missing binary or a failed admission self-test stops the Build before any launch,
   135	    naming the reason, and there is no unwrapped fallback. Both runtime-upgrade workflows re-run the
   136	    boundary probes, and a macOS upgrade on the Build host should too (README).
   137	
   138	- id: harness-write-drift
   139	  scenario_ids: [role-write-boundary, codex-roles-inside-boundary]
   140	  description: >-
   141	    The grants cover what Claude Code 2.1.281 and Codex 0.156.1 wrote in the probes. A new runtime
   142	    could write elsewhere, for example a new cache dir under the real HOME, and the role would then
   143	    fail on EPERM. Kogen gives no broader grant. Readiness runs inside the boundary, both
   144	    runtime-upgrade workflows re-probe, and the denial is logged by the kernel
   145	    (`log show --predicate 'eventMessage CONTAINS "deny(1) file-write"'`, named in README).
   146	    Denials of a role's own shell-profile writes (zsh completion caches, mise state under HOME) are
   147	    harmless and expected noise.
   148	
   149	- id: role-writable-login-state
   150	  scenario_ids: [role-write-boundary, codex-roles-inside-boundary]
   151	  description: >-
   152	    For logins to keep working, roles can write the login keychain file (Claude Code's OAuth
   153	    refresh runs /usr/bin/security in-process; probe 12), the Claude refresh lock, and most of the
   154	    Codex scope (auth.json refresh, rollouts, config.toml bookkeeping). A role could therefore add a
   155	    keychain item or corrupt its own login, but not take over another tool: Keychain item ACLs
   156	    still apply; the Codex discovery and Kogen-owned entries are denied; config.toml is validated
   157	    by native_settings.py at every Kogen open. Reads, including of credentials, are not confined by
   158	    this Intent (SEC-01 read isolation and SEC-02 are later).
   159	
   160	- id: controller-verification-unconfined
   161	  scenario_ids: [write-boundary-fails-closed, controller-judges-candidate]
   162	  description: >-
   163	    The controller runs `make check` and the selected targets on Candidate code outside the
   164	    boundary. A Developer can't confine that code, but it can write it, so a malicious test would
   165	    run with the user's full write access during verification. This is deliberate: fixture Builds
   166	    inside check and the live targets must apply their own profile, which the kernel refuses inside
   167	    another profile, and live targets must update logins and retained evidence. Review and the
   168	    guarded-path check see such code before publication; confining verification needs a
   169	    nesting-free design (for example per-target profiles with fixture Builds disabled) and belongs
   170	    with process custody (ROADMAP order 7).
   171	
   172	- id: inherited-mode
   173	  scenario_ids: [write-boundary-fails-closed]
   174	  description: >-
   175	    A Build whose controller already runs inside a Kogen role profile (a fixture Build started from
   176	    a Developer's shell, or mix kogen.expert from the Developer's tree) launches its roles without
   177	    its own profile and records `inherited`. It stays inside the enclosing profile, which the
   178	    kernel won't let it leave, but its grants are the enclosing Build's, not its own. Only the
   179	    kernel self-test plus the marker enables this mode; a foreign sandbox without the marker stops
   180	    the Build, and a marker without confinement is ignored.
   181	
   182	- id: unrun-live-targets
   183	  scenario_ids: [same-candidate-rework, per-build-harness-home]
   184	  description: >-
   185	    live-general runs native launches (no Build) that now go through the changed Claude
   186	    environment; it is not run here, and its owner file is not edited. live-reviewer-rework is now
   187	    selected (scenario codex-roles-inside-boundary), so its hybrid nested Build, with a worktree, a
   188	    per-Build home, the write boundary and a Codex Reviewer whose operation root is in that home,
   189	    has a real run in this Intent. The next Build that selects live-general is its first real run
   190	    on this code.
   191	
   192	- id: space-in-workspace-path
   193	  scenario_ids: [candidate-creation, same-candidate-rework, per-build-harness-home]
   194	  description: >-
   195	    The default root contains a space ("Application Support"). Any unquoted path in a Make recipe,
   196	    sh -c string, hook command or test helper breaks only in real use. test_helper.exs uses a
   197	    spaced root for every run, including the live fixture. Known instance:
   198	    test/kogen/lifecycle_test.exs:781-791 (install_target_evidence_fixture!/1, at 363c20af) splices unquoted -pa paths.
