=== harness core
     1	defmodule Kogen.Harness do
     2	  @moduledoc """
     3	  The one harness interface used by Build, the Shape task and provider evidence.
     4	
     5	  The session's resolved route (see `Kogen.Intent.read_config/2`) names its
     6	  harness. `codex` selects managed native Codex (`Kogen.Harness.Codex`);
     7	  `claude` selects the Kogen-managed Claude Code (`Kogen.Harness.Claude`). The
     8	  adapter supplies runtime and login readiness, launch contexts, fresh and
     9	  exactly resumed Developer turns, Reviewer verdicts and the interactive Shaper.
    10	
    11	  Every selection and launch context carries its harness explicitly, and
    12	  dispatch accepts only `claude` and `codex`: a missing or unknown harness
    13	  fails loudly. Every launch takes the session's launch context; nothing here
    14	  re-reads configuration. `Kogen.Check` and the Stop runner stay
    15	  harness-independent.
    16	
    17	  A route assigns each role (`shaping`, `developer`, `reviewer`, `expert`) a
    18	  harness. `open_roles/3` holds one selection per harness those roles use and
    19	  `role_context/2` launches each role only through its assigned harness, with
    20	  that harness's native helpers. A role whose Expert runs on another harness
    21	  reaches it through `mix kogen.expert`, never through a substituted native
    22	  helper; `expert_environment/2` carries the frozen Expert assignment.
    23	  """
    24	  use Boundary, deps: [Kogen.Codex, Kogen.ClaudeCode, Kogen.Intent]
    25	
    26	  alias Kogen.Harness.{Claude, Codex}
    27	
    28	  @expert_variable "KOGEN_EXPERT"
    29	
    30	  @doc "Opens readiness for the resolved route's harness only, before any launch."
    31	  def open(config, project \\ File.cwd!()) do
    32	    case harness(config) do
    33	      {:ok, "claude"} -> Kogen.ClaudeCode.open(config, project)
    34	      {:ok, "codex"} -> Kogen.Codex.open(config, project)
    35	      {:error, reason} -> {:error, reason}
    36	    end
    37	  end
